---
import MainLayout from "@/components/layout/MainLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "27 August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Small Web Apps handles your data: browser-only tool processing, hosting logs, cookies, Google AdSense advertising, and your privacy rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="static-page">
    <div class="static-inner">
      <span class="static-eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="static-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="static-card">
        <p>
          This policy explains what data Small Web Apps collects, what it does not collect, and how
          third parties — principally Google — use cookies and similar technologies when you visit
          this site. It applies to <strong>smallwebapps.com</strong> and every tool and guide page on it.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who runs this site</h2>
        <p>
          Small Web Apps is an independent project built and operated by <strong>Lucas Diniz</strong>
          as an individual, not as a registered company. For the purposes of the EU and UK GDPR, Lucas
          Diniz is the data controller for this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy questions and data requests:
          <!--email_off-->
          <a class="prose-link" href="mailto:lucas.hdo@hotmail.com">lucas.hdo@hotmail.com</a>
          <!--/email_off-->
          — see the <a class="prose-link" href="/contact/">Contact page</a> for other channels.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What the tools do with your files and text</h2>
        <p>
          Every tool on this site runs entirely inside your browser tab. When you select a file, paste
          text, or type into a tool, that content is processed locally using JavaScript and standard
          browser APIs. <strong>It is never uploaded to a server, never transmitted to us, and never
          stored by us.</strong> Closing or refreshing the tab discards it from memory.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a technical property of how the site is built, not just a promise: Small Web Apps is
          a static site with no application backend, no database, and no file-upload endpoint. If a
          future tool ever needs a network request to work, that tool's own page will say so explicitly
          in its limitations section.
        </p>

        <h2>3. What is collected automatically</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes standard
          request data in order to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. This typically includes:
        </p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>your IP address;</li>
          <li>your browser type, version, and operating system (user agent);</li>
          <li>the page URL you requested and the referring page, if any;</li>
          <li>the date and time of the request.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not maintain our own server logs, and we do not build profiles, accounts, or mailing
          lists from this data. Cloudflare's handling of it is governed by
          <a class="prose-link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          Small Web Apps itself sets no first-party tracking cookies. It uses your browser's local
          storage for two small preferences that never leave your device:
        </p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li><strong><code>swa-theme</code></strong> — remembers whether you chose light or dark mode.</li>
          <li><strong><code>swa_consent</code></strong> — remembers your choice from the cookie banner, so you are not asked again on every page.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Third-party cookies set by advertising are described in the next section. You can clear both
          local-storage values at any time through your browser's site-data settings.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to display advertising, which is what keeps the
          tools free to use. The following applies whenever ads are served:
        </p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>
            Third-party vendors, <strong>including Google</strong>, use cookies to serve ads based on your
            prior visits to this site or other sites.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on
            your visit to this and other sites on the internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            Third parties may also use web beacons, device identifiers, and your IP address to measure ad
            performance, limit how often you see the same ad, and detect invalid clicks or fraud.
          </li>
          <li>
            Where required by law, personalized advertising is only used after you consent through the
            cookie banner. If you decline, ads may still be shown but are non-personalized.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Advertising is never placed inside a tool's working area, and ads are never disguised as tool
          controls, navigation, or download buttons.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Small Web Apps does not currently run Google Analytics or any other visitor-analytics product.
          If that changes, this policy will be updated before analytics is enabled, and analytics storage
          will remain subject to the same consent choice as advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your choices and controls</h2>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>
            <strong>The cookie banner on this site</strong> — accept or decline advertising and analytics
            storage. Your choice is applied through Google Consent Mode, which defaults to <em>denied</em>
            until you choose otherwise.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="prose-link" href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>
            — review the interests Google associates with you and turn off personalized ads across Google services.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="prose-link" href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Network Advertising Initiative opt-out</a>
            — opt out of interest-based ads from participating NAI member networks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="prose-link" href="https://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Advertising Alliance WebChoices</a>
            — manage interest-based advertising from participating DAA companies.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="prose-link" href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads/anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's ads opt-out page</a>
            — opt out of personalized advertising served by Google specifically.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your browser</strong> — block or delete third-party cookies, or use private browsing.
            The tools on this site work normally with third-party cookies blocked.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. If you are in the EEA, UK, or Switzerland</h2>
        <p>
          Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, the legal basis for processing is:
          <strong>consent</strong> for advertising and analytics storage (Article 6(1)(a)), and
          <strong>legitimate interests</strong> for the security and delivery of the site
          (Article 6(1)(f)) — specifically, serving pages reliably and protecting the site from abuse.
        </p>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>request access to personal data held about you;</li>
          <li>request correction or erasure of that data;</li>
          <li>object to or request restriction of processing;</li>
          <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal;</li>
          <li>lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Because this site holds no accounts and no user database, in most cases the only personal data
          connected to you is held by Cloudflare and Google under their own policies. Requests sent to the
          contact address above will be answered, and pointed to the right controller where that applies.
        </p>

        <h2>9. If you are in California or another US state with privacy rights</h2>
        <p>
          Small Web Apps does not sell personal information and does not share it for cross-context
          behavioural advertising in exchange for money. Advertising cookies set by Google may still
          constitute "sharing" under the CPRA; declining through the cookie banner, or using Google's
          opt-out links above, is the way to limit that. You may also request to know, delete, or correct
          personal information by writing to the contact address above, and you will not be treated
          differently for exercising those rights.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is a general-audience developer and productivity toolset. It is not directed at
          children under 13 (or under 16 in the EEA/UK), and it does not knowingly collect personal
          information from them. Ad serving on this site is not configured as child-directed. If you
          believe a child has provided personal information here, contact us and it will be removed.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We hold no user database, so there is nothing on our side to retain or delete. Tool content
          exists only in your browser's memory for the duration of your session. Hosting request logs are
          retained by Cloudflare under its own retention schedule, and advertising data is retained by
          Google under Google's.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Some guides and tool pages link to external resources such as Google Takeout, documentation, or
          the project's GitHub repository. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and this policy
          does not cover them.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes materially — for example if analytics is introduced, or a tool begins
          sending data to a server — the "last updated" date at the top will change and the change will be
          described here. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept the revised policy.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy, or about how a specific tool handles data, can be sent to
          <!--email_off-->
          <a class="prose-link" href="mailto:lucas.hdo@hotmail.com">lucas.hdo@hotmail.com</a>
          <!--/email_off-->
          or raised on the
          <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/LucasHenriqueDiniz/smallwebapps/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">project issue tracker</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="static-highlight">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          <p>
            The short version: your files and text stay in your browser. What leaves your device is
            ordinary web-request data to the host, and advertising cookies you can decline.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
.static-page {
  max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 80px;
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}
.static-inner { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
.static-eyebrow {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
  background: rgba(26,115,232,.1); color: var(--blue);
  padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px;
  font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em;
  width: fit-content;
}
h1 {
  font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); font-weight: 900;
  color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -.5px; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0;
}
.static-meta {
  margin: -8px 0 0; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500;
}
.static-card {
  background: var(--surface-strong); border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 20px; padding: 32px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}
.static-card p {
  font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted); margin: 0;
}
.static-card h2 {
  font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text);
  margin: 18px 0 0; letter-spacing: -.2px;
}
.static-card h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 8px; }
.static-card code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  font-size: .85em; background: rgba(26,115,232,.08);
  padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; color: var(--blue);
}
.static-list {
  margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;
  font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted);
}
.static-list li { margin: 6px 0; }
.static-highlight {
  display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;
  background: rgba(26,115,232,.07); border: 1px solid rgba(26,115,232,.15);
  border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-top: 12px;
  color: var(--blue);
}
.static-highlight svg { flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
.static-highlight p  { color: var(--blue) !important; font-weight: 500; font-size: .88rem !important; line-height: 1.6 !important; }
</style>
